// Category: fatal errors — the run's outcome (exit code and error kind).
//
// An unguardable sources lemma aborts the proving run, even for a lemma
// simplification alone would close.
// No corpus theory fails this way.

// Category: proof corners no corpus proof reaches — a malformed `[sources]`
// lemma.
//
// The sources lemma cannot be converted to a guarded formula, but `done` is
// closed by simplification alone, which never forces the sources: the
// oracle proves `done` and leaves the sources lemma unproven.  No corpus
// theory has an unguardable sources lemma.

theory MalformedSources begin
rule R: [] --[ A() ]-> []
lemma typing [sources]: "All x #i. A() @ #i ==> x = x"
lemma done: "All #i. A() @ #i ==> A() @ #i"
end
